    "narrative": "For August 20th, our offensive core is headlined by **Lawrence Butler**, whose score of 73.47 makes him the premier start of the day. Facing Dobnak, **Lawrence Butler** benefits from a high-upside matchup against a sub-par 4.70 xERA starter, compounded by a strong spot in the #4 hole and a favorable park factor. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (69.84) and **Jonathan Aranda** (69.45) follow closely; **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains our most bankable asset, while **Jonathan Aranda** leverages a 19% boost from the opposing pitcher\u2019s inefficiency and a premium #3 lineup placement. **Daulton Varsho** (68.66) also warrants attention as a high-leverage play, utilizing a strong platoon advantage against the right-handed Rodriguez to maximize his power-speed profile.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved balancing the depth of our outfield against the bench. **JJ Bleday** squeezed into the final spot with a 51.44 score, narrowly edging out **Cal Raleigh**. While **Cal Raleigh** boasts a base projection of 58.75, his status as a non-starter today forced his efficiency score to zero, effectively sidelining him. We are monitoring **Jung Hoo Lee** (43.28) closely; while he is in the lineup, his low score is driven by a difficult matchup against Williams, who carries a tough 2.99 xERA, significantly capping **Jung Hoo Lee**'s ceiling. Elsewhere, **Dylan Beavers** (54.79) remains a high-risk, high-reward play\u2014his score is bolstered significantly by a +16% park factor, though he faces the sternest test of the day against Cole\u2019s 3.46 xERA. We continue to manage our remaining assets, including **Braden Montgomery** (53.24) and **Zack Gelof** (60.47), to ensure we maximize our category output without squandering games against elite arms.",
